
# syntactic equivalences


# passive -active
{
Mary ate the cake.
====
The cake was eaten.
>>> 1
}

{
Mary ate the cake.
====
The cake was not eaten by Mary.
>>> -1
}



# dative shift
{
Mary got the dog a book.
====
Mary got a dog to the book.
>>> 0
}


{
John gave the monkey a banana.
====
John gave a banana to the monkey.
>>> 1
}

{
Abby gave an apple to James.
====
Abby did not give James an apple.
>>> -1
}


# this syntax times out with the negation
{
Abby gave James an apple.
====
Abby did not give an apple to James.
>>> -1
}



# relative clauses

{
Abby finds a dog who ate a banana
====
A dog ate a banana.
>>> 1
}


{
Every red dog likes sausages.
====
Every dog who is red likes sausages.
>>> 1
}






